2026-06-22 17:05:25,620 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: To meet the City of Belval's technical requirements, we can leverage our experience in cloud architecture, AI/ML systems, and data engineering. Given our current technology stack, I propose designing an architecture based on the following components:

Firstly, to achieve a response time under 2 seconds, we can utilize our expertise in API integration and deploy the solution on a cloud provider with low latency, such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, which we have experience with. We can also employ containerization using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) to ensure efficient resource allocation and scalability.

Secondly, to integrate with the City of Belval's existing system of information, we can use our knowledge of API standards (REST, GraphQL, SOAP) and message brokers (Apache Kafka, RabbitMQ) to develop a seamless interface between our solution and their business softwares, electronic management of documents, and user directories.

Thirdly, to achieve high availability of at least 99.9%, we can design the architecture with redundancy and failover capabilities using Terraform for infrastructure-as-code (IaC) management and Ansible for configuration management. Our experience with monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack will also help us ensure proactive maintenance and quick issue resolution.

Lastly, to rely on infrastructures with low carbon impact, we can host the solution on SecNumCloud or an equivalent infrastructure, which aligns with our environmental optimization goals. We have experience with green hosting partners like OVHcloud (ISO 14001) and Scaleway (100% renewable), ensuring a reduced carbon footprint.

To ensure scalability, security, and sovereignty, we will implement the following measures:

* Use our expertise in cybersecurity to design a secure architecture with network segmentation, mTLS between services, and encryption (AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.3 in transit).
* Implement secrets management using HashiCorp Vault or CyberArk Conjur.
* Ensure data protection and sovereignty by hosting data within the European Union and complying with GDPR regulations.
* Provide regular training and support to City of Belval agents to ensure a smooth transition and optimal use of the solution.

By leveraging our technical expertise and experience, we can design an architecture that meets the City of Belval's technical requirements while ensuring scalability, security, and sovereignty. Our proposed solution will provide a fast, reliable, and environmentally friendly artificial intelligence solution that integrates seamlessly with their existing systems.
